Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission) prerequisite: add the
`object_layer_count` member to `LayerTools` in ToolOrdering.hpp.

FS v0.9.9's GCode emission code uses this field (alongside the
`mixed_mgr`, `num_physical`, `layer_index`, `print_z`,
`layer_height_for_mixed` members landed in patch 0019) to know the
total layer count for a print object when resolving virtual-row
cadence — it's referenced by the layer-cycle planner so the last few
layers can be biased toward a specific physical filament for clean
top-surface finishes.

Sole purpose: let the patch 0032 GCode emission port compile against
our v2.3.2 base. Defaults to 0, in which case
`LayerTools::resolve_mixed_1based()` (patch 0019) short-circuits to
identity — no behavior change on existing prints.

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/GCode/ToolOrdering.hpp b/src/libslic3r/GCode/ToolOrdering.hpp
index f78bf18aec..0acc40e107 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/GCode/ToolOrdering.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/GCode/ToolOrdering.hpp
@@ -168,6 +168,14 @@ public:
     // If per layer extruder switches are inserted by the G-code preview slider, this value contains the new (1 based) extruder, with which the whole object layer is being printed with.
     // If not overriden, it is set to 0.
     unsigned int 				extruder_override = 0;
+    // OrcaXR Android (FullSpectrum integration, patch 0028). Total number
+    // of object layers for the print object whose LayerTools this is —
+    // referenced by the FS v0.9.9 GCode emission patch's per-layer
+    // cadence resolver (matches PrintObject->layers().size() at the
+    // ToolOrdering construction site). Populated alongside layer_index
+    // by the planner; defaults to 0 when no mixed-filament manager is
+    // attached (in which case resolve_mixed_1based() short-circuits).
+    int                         object_layer_count = 0;
     // Should a skirt be printed at this layer?
     // Layers are marked for infinite skirt aka draft shield. Not all the layers have to be printed.
     bool                        has_skirt = false;
